{"title":"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> foot ladder is placed against a vertical wall of a building. The foot of the ladder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet from the base of the building. If the top of the ladder slips <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet, then the foot of the ladder will slide:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8028d4abfa584df9be7357f52423dde1ff28e7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 9\\text{ ft} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 15\\text{ ft} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 5\\text{ ft} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\text{ ft} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4\\text{ ft}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Pythag theorem, triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e283e9f3d92cd3c72f07c78e5cd8aba3010f8df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,24,25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, the point where the ladder meets the wall is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet above the ground. When the ladder slides, it becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet above the ground. By the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b192a9ad85a2e36e01833e29148dbfc8dd43c65c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(15,20,25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> Pythagorean triple, The foot of the ladder is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet from the building. Thus, it slides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4be2fff7b3ea82c4cc51cca4bd8f0b21f2d7d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15-7 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\text{ ft}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"146\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can observe that the above setup forms a right angled triangles whose base is 7ft and whose hypotenuse is 25ft taking the height to be x ft.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/36248f037e9b2e0f38f10e359a2daa98256920b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + 7^2 = 25^2\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/97315412dde7bf8656294fd50a3c4dd3beb6b60b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = 625 - 49\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e4004e971a834a0357d8333f6480c9125c376fbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = 576\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a18002296f7b456494f9ce99f7182976021f733.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 24\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since the top of the ladder slipped by 4 ft the new height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df5e694f2624efc6d4651b6611f29bb35d1b70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - 4 = 20 ft$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />. The base of the ladder has moved so the new base is say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f314e4e329015b475a73b4bcead37bf8080724f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />. The hypotenuse remains the same at 25ft. So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a33e5b4a4502e625193c88ea6deaa5d9d3e4c430.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20^2 + (7+y)^2 = 25^2\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd7346e90a6f0b66cf7ec5c9231c74964d7f6ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[400 + 49 + y^2 + 14y = 625\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6ed7dc729bec8d14653e2c3ba077cd557a70468.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 + 14y - 176 = 0\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb64cb6edd46acfc38c71de1a96b9b08ea3aa2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 + 22y - 8y - 176\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/795232f542208a287cf7e15269284ae365d84f73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x(y+22) - 8(y+22)\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e286f1276197ae2bdc9b0bc2cbeb2a52e59ff818.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(y-8)(y+22)\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Disregarding the negative solution to equation the solution to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/2861508ea6ef5a2163bf7cc2ac41bdd717e6c701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\text{ ft}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"74\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME\" title=\"1950 AHSME\">1950 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1950 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1950\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</